# Cursor Rules

Always read FORMETRIX.md before coding.

Follow these rules:
- Use TypeScript.
- Use Next.js.
- Use Supabase.
- Keep code modular.
- Avoid unnecessary libraries.
- Explain architectural tradeoffs.
- Do not expand Version 1 scope.
- Never fabricate business logic.

## Definition of Done (every engineering ticket) — FM-0028

A ticket may only be marked **Completed** after ALL of the following, in order.
Do not rely on memory; follow this list. See `docs/MISSION_CONTROL.md` §8.

1. Update the ticket's status and narrative source data (`management/data/tickets.json`, `management/TICKETS.md`, and any milestone narrative).
2. Run `npm run dashboard:update` to recompute calculated dashboard fields.
3. Run `npm run dashboard:check` — it must pass (no drift, no hard integrity errors).
4. Run `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run format:check`, and `npm run build` — all must pass.
5. Run `npm run dashboard:health` to record the real validation results into project health.
6. Append a `management/data/activity.json` entry and update `management/CHANGELOG.md`.
7. Only then set the ticket status to `completed`, and re-run `npm run dashboard:update` so current work and rollups reflect the closure.

Never claim a check passed without running it. Never hand-edit calculated dashboard fields — run the intelligence script instead.
